@startuml
title TMFC014 : Location Management -- eTOM/SID ABE Links
' TMFC014.md section 2.1 states no eTOM business activity is currently
' assigned to this component. Consistent with that, the source image does
' not name a real eTOM activity: both boxes are the literal placeholder
' text "L2 - New eTom Business Process" (reproduced verbatim, including its
' capitalization, as printed twice in the image -- distinct aliases used
' here only because PlantUML needs unique identifiers).

class "L2 - New eTom Business Process" as Placeholder1 <<eTOM Business Activity (placeholder)>>
class "L2 - New eTom Business Process" as Placeholder2 <<eTOM Business Activity (placeholder)>>
class "Location ABE" as LocationABE <<SID Data Entity>>

' Per the image's own legend: an arrow from an eTOM activity towards a SID
' ABE means the information is produced by the activity; the arrow in the
' other direction means the information is consumed by the activity. The
' image draws each side as a single double-headed arrow (arrowheads at both
' ends of one curved line), i.e. both hold simultaneously -- reproduced here
' as a pair of single-headed arrows per side, matching TMFC039's own
' redraw convention for the same visual pattern.
Placeholder1 --> LocationABE : produces
LocationABE --> Placeholder1 : is consumed by

LocationABE --> Placeholder2 : is consumed by
Placeholder2 --> LocationABE : produces

@enduml
